assistant: Subject: Accept epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order
Vendor API version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as a number of epoch milliseconds (e.g. `1792142857943`), but the published spec and the v1 fixtures use an ISO string. `get_order` always ran the value through `Date.parse(String(...))`, which returns NaN for a digit string. The `|| 0` fallback then turned that into the 1970-01-01 date the monitor caught. The fix, in `src/tools/get_order.ts`, uses a numeric `created_at` directly as milliseconds. ISO strings still go through the old path, so v1 output is unchanged. typecheck, lint and all 13 tests pass, but no test feeds the new numeric format, so that case wasn't run against the recorded response.

